   mock data, per CLAUDE.md's package structure (§3): "demo/ScreenA — sync
   dashboard demo, mock data, uses the shared library only." Consumes ONLY
   AppButton + MudBlazor's own layout components (MudStack/MudText) below —
   no page-specific CSS file, no hardcoded colors/px. Reference:
   demo/ScreenA/TaskOne_from_figma_design.png.

   FLAGGED — file placement/route: Pages/SyncStatus.razor already exists
   (currently just "@page \"/sync-status\"", an empty stub) and is the one
   AppSidebar's "حالة المزامنة" nav item actually links to
   (Components/AppSidebar.razor, Href="/sync-status"). That stub is left
   untouched — this file is a separate, additive demo route, matching how
   demo/FieldStatesGallery.razor works alongside AppField rather than
   replacing anything. Route chosen as "/demo/sync-status" (mirrors the real
   page's name under the /demo/ prefix) rather than "/demo/screen-a" (would
   mirror the ScreenA/ folder name instead) — flag if you'd rather the other
   name, or want this wired into Pages/SyncStatus.razor directly instead of
   living as a separate demo route.

   SCOPE — this step adds the filter row (see FILTER ROW note below) on top
   of the two Figma banner buttons wired earlier. The three status cards and
   sync health cards further down are still out of scope, per instruction,
   shown only as a single caption line below — building those now would be
   guessing at card chrome that doesn't exist in components.css yet (still
   listed as TODO there).

   ============================================================================
   FILTER ROW — new .app-panel + .app-filters-row section, AppField only
   ============================================================================
   Container: .app-panel (components.css) — new shared bordered/rounded card
   class, backed by new --panel-* tokens in tokens.css (flagged there: no
   existing token fit padding/radius/stroke exactly, --panel-color-stroke
   deliberately re-derives the same raw --color-lightgray-de value
   --sidebar-color-stroke already uses, rather than referencing that Token
   directly, per tokens.css's own "Tokens reference Variables, not other
   Tokens" convention). UPDATED in a later pass (see the "Sync-actions row +
   status card rows" restructuring below): the two banner cells no longer
   apply .app-panel directly — that border now lives on their shared outer
   .app-sync-actions-row wrapper instead (one panel for both cells, per
   TaskOne_Tablet.png), with each cell falling back to its own .app-panel-cell
   look only below 600px. .app-panel itself is unchanged and still backs
   this filter row exactly as originally built.

   Layout: .app-filters-row (components.css) — 4 equal columns via CSS Grid,
   collapsing to 1 column below the existing --breakpoint-sm (600px) token
   (the same one AppHeader already collapses its sync-button label at —
   reused rather than inventing a second breakpoint value). No separate
   tablet rule: verified live (see the browser check appended to this file's
   companion notes) that 4 equal 1fr columns simply narrow together above
   600px with no wrap/overflow, so tablet needed no rule of its own.

   Options data: fields 1-2 (تصفية حسب المركز / سلسلة الاختبار) pass an
   EMPTY Options list, each flagged with an inline comment — no venue/series
   list is wired up yet, per instruction, not an oversight. Field 3 (نوع
   الشغل) gets a small mock Options list purely so its already-selected
   value ("يومي") is a real member of the list, also flagged as mock.

   DOM order vs. the Figma's left-to-right reading order: written in
   RIGHT-to-left DOM order (تاريخ الاختبار, نوع الشغل, سلسلة الاختبار,
   تصفية حسب المركز) — the same "plain DOM order, first child renders at
   the RTL start/right edge" convention already used by AppHeader.razor and
   the button-banner stack above, driven by the app's single ambient
   dir="rtl" (MainLayout, CLAUDE.md §2), not a hardcoded physical side here.

   Date field: DateValue is the literal 2026/09/10 shown in the Figma
   screenshot. dir="ltr" is passed via AppField's InputAttributes
   passthrough (the only hook AppField exposes; restructuring the component
   to inject a literal `<span dir="ltr">` inside MudDatePicker's own
   rendered value would violate CLAUDE.md rule 7). CONFIRMED per CLAUDE.md
   rule 1 — not a guess: ran the built app (dotnet run + Playwright/headless
   Chromium) and read the live outerHTML of this exact field. UserAttributes
   lands `dir="ltr"` directly on the innermost
   <input class="mud-input-slot ..."> that actually carries the date text
   (id="mudinput..."), not on some outer wrapper — the ideal placement, since
   the label ("تاريخ الاختبار", correctly still unset/ambient-RTL) is a
   sibling <label> element, not part of that input. Screenshot confirms the
   rendered value reads "2026/09/10" left-to-right, not reordered. *@
@page "/demo/sync-status"

<PageTitle>Screen A — حالة المزامنة (demo)</PageTitle>

<MudStack Spacing="6" Class="pa-4">
    @* <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">حالة المزامنة</MudText> *@

    <div class="app-panel app-filters-row">
        <AppField T="string" Type="AppFieldType.Date" Label="تاريخ الاختبار"
                  DateValue="@_examDate" DateValueChanged="@(d => _examDate = d)"
                  InputAttributes="@_ltrDateAttributes" />
        <AppField T="string" Type="AppFieldType.Select" Label="نوع الشغل"
                  Value="@_shiftType" ValueChanged="@(v => _shiftType = v)"
                  Options="@_shiftTypeOptions" />
        <AppField T="string" Type="AppFieldType.Select" Label="سلسلة الاختبار"
                  Value="@_examSeries" ValueChanged="@(v => _examSeries = v)"
                  Options="@_emptyOptions" />
        <AppField T="string" Type="AppFieldType.Select" Label="تصفية حسب المركز"
                  Value="@_centerFilter" ValueChanged="@(v => _centerFilter = v)"
                  Options="@_emptyOptions" />
    </div>

    @* Row order matches the Figma reference read right-to-left: the
       "manual sync, all centers" cell sits first in DOM order so it renders
       on the right under the app's ambient dir="rtl" (MudRTLProvider, set
       once at MainLayout per CLAUDE.md §2) — same "plain DOM order, no
       row-reverse" approach already documented in AppHeader.razor.

       RESTRUCTURED TWICE this pass:
       1. Was originally a MudStack Row+Wrap, wrapping purely on intrinsic
          content width with no explicit breakpoint — found to wrap to
          stacked too early at tablet widths (~929px). Replaced with an
          explicit grid (.app-sync-actions-row, components.css), same
          --breakpoint-sm (600px) mechanism the other rows already use.
       2. CORRECTED after re-comparing directly against the Figma reference
          again (superseding an earlier two-separate-panels reading this
          conversation had settled on): the two banners and the 3-card CBT
          row below them are ONE single continuous .app-panel
          (.app-sync-block, components.css), not two. Internal separation is
          divider LINES only (border-inline-end between the two banners,
          border-block-end between this row and the card row below, and
          border-inline-end again between the three cards) — never a gap
          between separate boxes. Below 600px this still neutralizes back to
          individually-boxed stacked cells, matching TaskOne_Mobile.png
          (unchanged by this correction, that reference wasn't in question). *@
    <div class="app-panel app-sync-block">
        <div class="app-sync-actions-row" style="--app-sync-actions-row-count: 2">
            @* Rebuilt as AppActionBanner (Components/AppActionBanner.razor,
               Figma component "btn_box") — see that component's own header
               comment for the full anatomy/color-sync/specificity reasoning.
               Bordered="false" on both: this row already sits inside the
               shared .app-panel/.app-sync-block above, which supplies the
               border; see the component's own flagged note on why this
               deviates from the "btn_box" screenshot's own independent-card
               look. Badge icon corrected to Sync (was People, an unconfirmed
               placeholder from before this reference existed) — the actual
               screenshot shows the circular refresh glyph, not a people
               icon; that's now hardcoded inside AppActionBanner itself,
               matching every instance, not passed per-call. *@
            <AppActionBanner Title="مزامنة يدوية لجميع المراكز"
                              Description="وصف المزامنة اليدوية"
                              ButtonLabel="بدء المزامنة اليدوية"
                              Bordered="false" />

            <AppActionBanner Title="مزامنة إجابات المرشحين للتقييم يدويا"
                              Description="بدء مزامنة إجابات المرشحين للتقييم المحدد للتاريخ إلى نظام التقييم يدويا"
                              ButtonLabel="بدء مزامنة إجابات المرشحين"
                              Bordered="false" />
        </div>

        @* ====================================================================
           STATUS CARD ROW (3 cards) — new AppStatusCard.razor. See that
           component's own header comment for the full anatomy/color-mapping
           reasoning — only Title/Icon/ProgressPercent/StatusType/
           StatusLabel/MetaRows differ per card. Bordered="false" on every
           card here: this row is nested inside .app-sync-block above, which
           supplies the single shared .app-panel border for the whole block
           (banners + this row); see AppStatusCard.razor's Bordered param
           doc and components.css's "Sync-actions block" section.

           ALL numbers/labels/meta text below are MOCK/PLACEHOLDER data read
